[ADDTEXT] TRN_MISSION_01 "Free flight without threats to allow you to get used to handling the F-16."
[ADDTEXT] TRN_MISSION_02 "You are lined up on the runway, ready for take off. Practice your take off techniques."
[ADDTEXT] TRN_MISSION_03 "Familiarize yourself with F-16 capabilities at corner airspeed. Use ACMI to check your performance. Note max G's, turn rate and turn radius."
[ADDTEXT] TRN_MISSION_04 "Get familiar with F-16 performance above corner airspeed. Use ACMI to note increased turn radius and the decrease in turn rate as compared to corner airspeed."
[ADDTEXT] TRN_MISSION_05 "Get familiar with F-16 performance below corner airspeed. Use ACMI to note decreased turn radius, available G's and turn rate as compared to corner airspeed."
[ADDTEXT] TRN_MISSION_06 "Using the lessons learned in the corner airspeed scenarios, complete a Split S manuever and note how airspeed control affects your recovery altitude."
[ADDTEXT] TRN_MISSION_07 "Basically the opposite of a split S, ending up in the opposite direction at a higher altitude."
[ADDTEXT] TRN_MISSION_08 "Learn how airspeed, G load and altitude affect the handling of your jet."
[ADDTEXT] TRN_MISSION_09 "You are on an extended final approach. Carefully manage your airspeed, line up with the runway and practice the all important flare before touch down."
[ADDTEXT] TRN_MISSION_10 "Guide your jet to a landing using instruments only. Keys to success are smooth, timely inputs and an efficient cross check of the important instruments."
[ADDTEXT] TRN_MISSION_11 "You can safely land even without engine.  Use manual gear lever alt-g. This is a balancing act between airspeed and altitude."
[ADDTEXT] TRN_MISSION_12 "This is a skill you need for combat missions where you must get your bombs on target, on time. Use the avionics in the jet and control your airspeed and heading to fly a precise route."
[ADDTEXT] TRN_MISSION_13 "Master all of the different radar submodes here. Learn how to use azimuth and bar scan techniques to scour the skies for bandits."
[ADDTEXT] TRN_MISSION_14 "There's no kill like a guns kill and that's all you've got here."
[ADDTEXT] TRN_MISSION_15 "Learn to use rear and all aspect heat seeking missiles."
[ADDTEXT] TRN_MISSION_16 "Fly Training flight. Learn to use your AIM-120 missile to engage a wide variety of targets. Manage your Wingman and use AWACS as needed."
[ADDTEXT] TRN_MISSION_17 "An older generation radar guided missile, the Sparrow requires you to hold a solid lock from launch to impact."
[ADDTEXT] TRN_MISSION_18 "This mission will teach you the complex task of using your air-to-ground radar. This is a critical skill for many other air-to-ground weapons modes."
[ADDTEXT] TRN_MISSION_19 "This is the most important air-to-ground bombing mode. It is used as a submode in many of the other bombing modes."
[ADDTEXT] TRN_MISSION_20 "The CCIP pipper will tell you where the bomb will hit when you pickle."
[ADDTEXT] TRN_MISSION_21 "Practice with this stand off delivery technique to avoid deadly ground fire."
[ADDTEXT] TRN_MISSION_22 "A steady hand and good eyes are the order of the day, but watch the ground or you'll be a part of it."
[ADDTEXT] TRN_MISSION_23 "Pick out your target early and shoot straight. It takes time for an entire pod to ripple fire."
[ADDTEXT] TRN_MISSION_24 "Tanks moving, use GMT radar. Try SP mode and range. Practice Zoom and EXP. If uncertain of target, lock it and ask AWACS to Declare."
[ADDTEXT] TRN_MISSION_25 "Targets are acquired much like Mavericks, but you still have to drop it like an unguided bomb using CCRP mode."
[ADDTEXT] TRN_MISSION_26 "Wiley SAM operators likely to turn on and off their scan radar. The AGM-88 works best against a radiating radar. Listen for 'Mud' calls."
[ADDTEXT] TRN_MISSION_27 "Patience will never be rewarded so much as when you are within arms reach of a tanker. Smooth, easy inputs and good formation skills are needed here."
[ADDTEXT] TRN_MISSION_28 "To the North is an SA-8, east is an SA-13, the south is blocked by an Alamo carrying Mig-29, and west is the venerable SA-2."
[ADDTEXT] TRN_MISSION_29 "Learn the fine art of flying to the elbow and gain mastery over any enemy."
[ADDTEXT] TRN_MISSION_30 "J-11 on your six! He's got HOJ AA-10A missiles so keep your jammer off. His doppler radar is not fooled by chaff so you have to out-run & out-turn the missiles. Dive low, defeat the missiles & smoke this amatuer!"
[ADDTEXT] TRN_MISSION_31 "Also known as the merge, almost every BFM engagement you'll have begins here. Gain the advantage by learning how to deal with this setup."
